00:00:00.679 --> 00:00:04.680
Hello and welcome to this video in which
we'll look at the factors to be considered

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.220
when selecting a work area for an activity.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.649
So how do you choose where
to set up a work activity?

00:00:11.184 --> 00:00:16.305
Is it just where's most convenient, sufficient
space, or where the mess won't get in the way?

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:20.165
Do you think about what's needed for
the activity and create the space

00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:21.835
specifically with this in mind?

00:00:23.285 --> 00:00:27.704
This video will look at why it's important
that the area selected for a work activity

00:00:27.944 --> 00:00:31.714
should be carefully chosen and what
to consider when making your decision.

00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:41.664
We will look at health and safety, cleanliness,
product quality, accessibility, and noise

00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:43.674
levels and environmental conditions.

00:00:45.654 --> 00:00:50.114
Perhaps the most important factor to consider
when selecting a work area is safety.

00:00:50.664 --> 00:00:54.284
The area should be free from hazards
that could cause injury or damage.

00:00:55.035 --> 00:01:00.455
The work area should have adequate lighting,
ventilation, and access to emergency exits.

00:01:01.014 --> 00:01:06.225
Consider whether the area has any flammable
materials, toxic substances, or electrical

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.644
hazards that could put the workers at risk.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:12.874
Are items that are needed stored
safely, but easy to reach?

00:01:13.565 --> 00:01:16.774
Do any of them need special storage
due to their hazardous nature?

00:01:17.339 --> 00:01:21.630
Is there room for additional safety equipment
if needed such as fire extinguishers?

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:27.769
It's important that all work areas can
be kept clean as this reduces the risk of

00:01:27.769 --> 00:01:32.789
contamination and bacterial infection, which
is part of the Health and Safety at Work

00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:36.019
Act 1974, which we looked at in Unit 1.

00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:39.875
When considering where a work activity
should take place, you should think

00:01:39.885 --> 00:01:41.795
about how easy it is to be cleaned.

00:01:42.574 --> 00:01:46.174
Can work surfaces be cleared for
cleaning and are bins nearby?

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:51.725
Also think about how workers will access bathrooms
and kitchen facilities, and how close these

00:01:51.725 --> 00:01:54.394
should be, which will depend on the work involved.

00:01:55.085 --> 00:01:59.645
Some activities aren't suitable to drink
or snack on the job, so in this case can

00:01:59.645 --> 00:02:04.085
workers easily access another area where
they can make a drink or eat a snack.

00:02:05.405 --> 00:02:10.074
Accessibility is also an important factor
to consider when selecting a work area.

00:02:10.685 --> 00:02:14.515
You should choose a location that is
easily accessible by the workers and

00:02:14.515 --> 00:02:16.335
the materials needed for the activity.

00:02:16.894 --> 00:02:22.085
Also, consider whether there are any restrictions
on access to the area, such as during

00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:25.114
certain times of the day or on specific days.

00:02:25.714 --> 00:02:29.044
Think about how many people may
need access at any given time.

00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:30.795
Is there space for them all?

00:02:31.365 --> 00:02:35.955
Can you make the space fully accessible for
anyone using aids, such as a wheelchair?

00:02:37.809 --> 00:02:42.160
The noise level of the work area is also
an important factor to consider that

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.000
some activities can produce a lot of
noise which can be distracting or even

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.790
harmful to the hearing of the workers.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:53.860
It's important to assess the noise level and take
measures to reduce it if necessary, such as using

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.780
earplugs, ear masks or sound absorbing materials.

00:02:58.505 --> 00:03:02.045
Conversely, does the area allow
for everyone to hear what's needed?

00:03:02.635 --> 00:03:06.135
Many customer areas now have
hearing loop facilities installed.

00:03:06.625 --> 00:03:08.135
Will your work area need this?

00:03:08.695 --> 00:03:12.504
Do you have a quiet area where discussions
can take place without the need

00:03:12.505 --> 00:03:14.495
shout over loud machinery or people?

00:03:16.355 --> 00:03:19.725
The environmental conditions of
the work area are also important.

00:03:20.485 --> 00:03:24.954
You should consider factors such as
temperature, humidity, and air quality.

00:03:25.525 --> 00:03:29.174
Some activities require specific
environmental conditions to function

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:33.584
properly, so it's important to choose a
work area that meets these requirements.

00:03:34.225 --> 00:03:36.445
Lighting is important for all tasks.

00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:41.635
If there's natural light in the area, is
the workstation placed in the correct place?

00:03:42.185 --> 00:03:47.415
For example, think about DSE guidance for where
a monitor should be placed with a nearby window.

00:03:47.995 --> 00:03:52.485
If there's no natural light, is the lighting
installed correct for the work activity?

00:03:54.345 --> 00:03:58.975
Product quality will differ greatly depending
on the product you are producing in your area.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:03.269
For example, is the area making
a small part of a bigger item?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:07.589
Is it seating for laptop users
or an area to meet with clients?

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:12.419
Whatever the reason, when setting up your
work activity, it is important that you

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:17.269
consider the product or service quality and
that the space is suitable for its needs.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.750
For example, if it's meeting with clients,
being on the top floor of a high building

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.810
with no lift may not be the best place.

00:04:25.395 --> 00:04:28.515
If it's producing an item,
there is more to consider.

00:04:28.925 --> 00:04:33.765
It's no use having a state of the art setup
if the position of the work activity makes

00:04:33.765 --> 00:04:38.765
it difficult for workers to use the necessary
machinery and link in with other production needs.

00:04:39.365 --> 00:04:44.235
Everything we've considered in this video leads
to the production of quality products or services.

00:04:44.645 --> 00:04:49.045
Without this the customer won't be
satisfied and you've wasted time and effort.

00:04:49.815 --> 00:04:53.585
In conclusion, we can see that it's
not just a case of setting up a work

00:04:53.585 --> 00:04:55.905
activity in whatever space is available.

00:04:56.465 --> 00:05:01.385
We've highlighted just a few considerations
in this video which really shows, if you want

00:05:01.385 --> 00:05:06.515
the space to be optimized, usable and deliver
quality, there are many factors to consider.

